      "message": "e_price`, but **I could not confirm those checks actually ran**:\n\n- Several `run_command` calls returned `{\"ok\": true}` with empty stdout even though they contained `print` statements and one contained a deliberate `ModuleNotFoundError`; the identical command later genuinely failed with `returncode: 1`. So `ok: true` with empty stdout is not reliable evidence in this environment.\n- One check reported `'No module named producer'`, proving the attempt-directory path I passed was wrong (the real path is `attempts/A_direct_attempt_1`).\n- I tried writing `check_result.txt` and `probe.txt`; **neither file exists** when read back, so those commands did not take effect.\n\nI therefore make **no claim** that the parity check passed. The semantics are correct by direct textual copy of the v1 expression, and I verified the file contents via `read_file`, but the dynamic equivalence test is unverified. Only `producer.py` should be treated as written; the check-result and probe files were not created."
